{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-29_entgq32026ex991.htm, sha256 7526dac7dbe6a1cd3a14e74c8455c13fc38ab2050926bd4b6a96c47cd85d22cf.\nEX-99.1 2 entgq32026ex991.htm EX-99.1\nPRESS RELEASE\nJeffrey Schnell Vice President, Investor Relations T + 1 201 207 3029 jeffrey.schnell@entegris.com\nExhibit 99.1\nENTEGRIS REPORTS RESULTS FOR THIRD QUARTER OF 2026\n\u2022Net sales of $1,006 million. \u2022GAAP diluted EPS of $1.03. \u2022Non-GAAP diluted EPS of $1.23.\nBILLERICA, Mass., October 29, 2026 - Entegris, Inc. (NASDAQ: ENTG), today reported its financial results for the Company\u2019s third quarter ended September 26, 2026. Dave Reeder, Entegris\u2019 President and Chief Executive Officer, said: \u201cEntegris is executing well against an attractive long-term opportunity, driven by increasing semiconductor complexity, rising materials intensity, and investment in leading-edge technologies. Our ability to deliver the performance, quality, and reliability our customers require is helping us expand plans of record and secure new design wins, driving strong revenue growth across our unit and capex businesses. That growth, combined with disciplined execution, drove another strong quarter, highlighted by record revenue, continued margin expansion and strong earnings growth, all of which exceeded our guidance range. We also delivered record cash flow, enabling us to accelerate debt repayment and further strengthen our balance sheet. We look forward to discussing the significant opportunities ahead for Entegris and our long-term strategy in more detail at our Capital Markets Day on November 9, 2026.\u201d\nQuarterly Financial Results Summary (in millions, except percentages and per share data)\nGAAP Results Sep 26, 2026 Sep 27, 2025 Jun 27, 2026\nNet sales $1,005.7 $807.1 $883.2\nGross margin - as a % of net sales 49.7 % 43.5 % 47.6 %\nOperating margin - as a % of net sales 22.9 % 15.2 % 18.6 %\nNet income $157.8 $70.5 $93.6\nDiluted earnings per common share $